      "Saint Capitolina and Saint Erotheis": 1,
      "Capitolina and her maidservant Erotheis were martyred in Cappadocia, in present-day Turkey. According to tradition, they died in the persecution under Emperor Diocletian, around 304. Their feast is kept on October 27 in the Catholic, Orthodox, Armenian and Syriac Orthodox calendars.": 1,
      "Brief story based on Catholic Online and the Ecumenical Saints Lexicon.": 1,
      "Read about Saint Capitolina": 1,
