      "31 Oct": 1,
      "Saints Cosmas and Damian": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar lists Saints Cosmas and Damian, martyrs, on November 1 without details. On name and date this entry fits the Byzantine feast of the Unmercenary Physicians Cosmas and Damian, kept on November 1. According to their traditional life, the twin brothers were raised in Christian piety in Asia Minor by their mother, Saint Theodota. Trained as physicians, they healed illnesses of body and soul by the power of prayer and never accepted payment, following the Lord's command, 'Freely have you received, freely give.' The brothers reposed in peace and were buried together at Thereman. The Orthodox Church distinguishes three pairs of saints named Cosmas and Damian; the Western Church keeps the better-known martyr twins on September 26.": 1,
      "Brief story based on Wikipedia and the Orthodox Church in America. The date follows the Maronite calendar.": 1,
      "Read about Saints Cosmas and Damian": 1,
